# Credentials for the test run only — deliberately committed, deliberately fake.
#
# `src/shared/lib/supabase.ts` throws at import time when these two are
# missing, so every test file that reaches the client — directly or through a
# hook — fails to load without them. `.env.local` is git-ignored, so a fresh
# clone, a git worktree and CI all lack it, and the suite that passes on the
# author's machine does not run anywhere else. That gap has already cost this
# project once: every early bundle baseline was measured in a worktree without
# `.env.local`, which let the bundler dead-code-eliminate all of
# `@supabase/supabase-js`, and two wrong figures were reported before anyone
# noticed.
#
# Vitest runs in mode `test`, so Vite loads this file automatically and
# `.env.local` still wins locally when it exists.
#
# No test may talk to this host: the URL points nowhere and the key is not a
# credential. Anything that needs a real database is a pgTAP test under
# `supabase/tests/`, run by `npm run test:db`.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=http://localhost:54321
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=test-anon-key-not-a-credential
